  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": "Replaces Colorado's flat individual income-tax rate with a graduated-rate structure and increases state taxes by an estimated $2.7 billion annually. The law would direct additional revenue to K-12 education, health care, and early child care and education. Amendment 87 conflicts with Proposition 136, which caps the income tax rate at 4.4%. If both measures pass, Colorado's rules governing conflicting measures would apply.",
