        "version": 1
      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "detail": 0,
            "format": 8,
            "mode": "normal",
            "style": "",
            "text": "Section 20. THE TAXPAYER’S BILL OF RIGHTS",
            "type": "extended-text",
            "version": 1
          }
        ],
        "direction": "ltr",
        "format": "",
        "indent": 0,
        "type": "link",
        "version": 1,
        "rel": null,
        "target": null,
        "title": null,
        "url": "https://advance.lexis.com/documentpage/?pdmfid=1000516&crid=b75fd404-e45d-46e3-b86c-ef7854525028&nodeid=AABAALAAW&nodepath=%2FROOT%2FAAB%2FAABAAL%2FAABAALAAW&level=3&haschildren=&populated=false&title=Section+20.+THE+TAXPAYER%E2%80%99S+BILL+OF+RIGHTS&config=0143JAAwODgxYWIyNi1mNGJlLTQwYmItYmE4Ni0yOWY2NzQzMjE3MTAKAFBvZENhdGFsb2ecqetP0coiYGhC4QCG46NJ&pddocfullpath=%2Fshared%2Fdocument%2Fstatutes-legislation%2Furn%3AcontentItem%3A61VF-9YD1-DYDC-J53M-00008-00&ecomp=6gf5kkk&prid=4c215efd-9971-41a1-aa1c-7a1d9c2f51a0"
      },
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": ") locking in a regressive income tax system for the past 30+ years. That meant that whether you were making $30,000 a year or $3,000,000 per year, you would pay the same 4.4% of your income in tax to the State of Colorado. Such a system makes it more difficult for people with median or lower incomes to afford basic necessities like housing, transportation, child care, and food. But also in recent years, it means that as inequality has grown, we are also starving our state budget which needs to provide basic services like public schools, health care, and child care. Amendment 87 intends to address this problem directly.",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
